---
name: upgrade-sc-compose
version: 2.1.0
description: Unattended sc-compose upgrade - edit the repo pin, handle the changelog, test old against new, PR, and release when nothing else is in flight.
format: toml
required_variables:
  - parent
  - ref
  - phase
  - from_version
  - to_version
  - priority
---
{#
sc-compose beads formula (sc-compose/beads/v1), attached with
`sc-compose bead attach` under the phase root of one upgrade run. Poured ids
are <parent>.<ref>-<step>.

The repo pin is the only version this formula changes. Other skills and kits
declare their own minimum versions and are not edited here. The run needs no
input from Rand; every decision, stop and escalation goes to omega-prime@hermes
with `atm send omega-prime@hermes --stdin <<'EOF'` (never an inline quoted
body: substituted PR text may contain backticks).

Sample requests for deliverable 5 live in upgrade-sc-compose.samples/.
`sc-compose bead` exits 0 on refusal; read payload.outcome, never the exit code.
#}
formula = "upgrade-sc-compose"
description = "Upgrade sc-compose {{{ from_version }}} -> {{{ to_version }}} (phase-{{{ phase }}})."
version = 2
type = "workflow"

[[steps]]
id = "sprint"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: sprint {{{ phase }}}-1 sc-compose {{{ to_version }}}"
description = "Sprint container for the sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade. Its deliverables are on {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-upgrade; QA fix groups attach under this bead. Container only: do not dispatch it. The lead closes it when {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa closes."
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:sprint"]

[steps.metadata]
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ phase }}}-1"
stack = "phase-{{{ phase }}}"
layer = 1
difficulty = "fast"

[[steps]]
id = "upgrade"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: pin sc-compose {{{ to_version }}}"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. `.claude/lib/sc_compose_dependency.py`: `SC_COMPOSE_PIN` and the `sc-compose==` install pin read {{{ to_version }}}. Minimum-version constants are not changed.
2. Read randlee/sc-compose at tag v{{{ to_version }}}: every `CHANGELOG.md` section after {{{ from_version }}} up to {{{ to_version }}}, `docs/migration-notes.md` and `docs/migration/`. List each breaking change, deprecation and recommended change in this bead's notes. For each one, `git grep` the repo for the affected command, flag, API or template syntax and either (a) apply the change to the repo-owned use in this layer, covered by deliverable 4 or 5, and list the changed path in the notes, or (b) record "not used" with the grep. A use in a kit- or other-skill-owned file is not edited: file a GitHub issue against the owning repo, link it in the notes, and send omega-prime@hermes the issue link.
3. Two scratch environments: A = a worktree at this layer's base commit (before deliverables 1-2) with sc-compose {{{ from_version }}}; B = this layer's head with sc-compose {{{ to_version }}}. Each has the release CLI binary first on PATH and `pip install sc-compose==<v>` in its own venv. Record `sc-compose --version` and the wheel version in each; a mismatch voids the run.
4. In A and in B, run `python3 -m pytest -q .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/tests .claude/skills/atm-beads/tests .claude/skills/triaging-findings/tests bindings/sc-lint-py/python/sc_lint/tests/test_orchestration_contracts.py` and record pass/fail per test id.
5. In A and in B, run `sc-compose bead validate --request <f> --json` for each file in `.atm-bd/formula/upgrade-sc-compose.samples/`. For the upgrade-sc-compose sample, B renders A's copy of this formula (the base commit's), so an edit made under deliverable 8 is not a difference. Record each payload.outcome, then diff each rendered formula under `target/upgrade-samples/` byte for byte between A and B.
6. Verdict in this bead's notes: BREAKING when a test passing in A fails in B, a sample's outcome differs, or a rendered formula differs between A and B; list each with its output or diff. A test failing in both is pre-existing and reported, not breaking. NOT BREAKING otherwise.
7. With B installed, `just lint` and `just test` pass.
8. `git grep -n "sc-compose==\\|SC_COMPOSE_PIN"` finds no repo-owned pin other than deliverable 1; any new one is listed in the notes and added to this formula's deliverable 1.

If the run cannot be done (tag or release asset missing, an environment will not install, a void version match), record the refusal in the notes, send omega-prime@hermes the reason, and leave this bead open.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:dev"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "dev"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
stack = "phase-{{{ phase }}}"
layer = 1
difficulty = "fast"
sprint = "{{{ phase }}}-1"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sprint"
branch = "sprint/{{{ phase }}}-1-sc-compose-{{{ to_version }}}"
pr_target = "integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}}"
owned_paths = [".claude/lib/sc_compose_dependency.py"]

[[steps]]
id = "sanity"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: sanity check"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. Sanity check of {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-upgrade: each numbered deliverable is written and lint passes. This is not QA.

Close on PASS only; on FAIL reopen the upgrade bead, leave this bead open, and send omega-prime@hermes the failing deliverables.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:dev-sanity"]
needs = ["upgrade"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "dev-sanity"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
stack = "phase-{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ phase }}}-1"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sprint"
dev_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-upgrade"
difficulty = "fast"

[[steps]]
id = "qa"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: QA sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} pin"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. quality-mgr checks the upgrade bead's changelog list against the sc-compose CHANGELOG and migration docs (each item applied, not used, or issued), re-runs deliverables 3-6 independently with the same sample requests, and confirms the recorded versions, per-test results, rendered diffs and verdict match. The diff holds only the pin and the deliverable 2 paths listed in the notes. CI on the layer is green or its failure is a recorded breaking change.

On FAIL: file the findings as fix beads per atm-bd-orchestration, leave this bead open until a fix round passes re-QA, and send omega-prime@hermes the findings.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:qa"]
needs = ["sanity"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "qa"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
stack = "phase-{{{ phase }}}"
round = 1
difficulty = "normal"
sprint = "{{{ phase }}}-1"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sprint"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-upgrade"

[[steps]]
id = "pr_develop"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: PR to develop"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. Land the layer on integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}} (`gh stack merge <stack> --yes --merge`), open the ready integrate/phase-{{{ phase }}} -> develop PR, and request review from `rand-lee` (`gh api -X POST repos/randlee/sc-lint/pulls/<n>/requested_reviewers -f 'reviewers[]=rand-lee'`). Never merge it; only Rand merges to develop.
2. Decision point 1. BREAKING (upgrade verdict): put the verdict, failing tests and diffs in the PR description; close `{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-release` as not planned; send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade is BREAKING. Rand, please review <PR link>." with the failing tests. NOT BREAKING: when CI is green, send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} upgrade, CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>.". If CI cannot go green, send omega-prime@hermes the failing check and leave this bead open.
3. Keep this bead open until Rand merges the PR. When omega-prime or Rand reports the merge, confirm it with one REST read (`gh api repos/randlee/sc-lint/pulls/<n> --jq .merged`), then close this bead. No polling. This bead is open by design while it waits for the merge; do not re-dispatch it.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:land"]
needs = ["qa"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "lead"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"

[[steps]]
id = "release"
title = "phase-{{{ phase }}}: patch release PR to main"
description = """
## Deliverables
1. Decision point 2. Other work in progress = an open phase or release bead other than {{{ parent }}} and its children, or another open PR to develop. If there is any, send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: sc-compose {{{ to_version }}} on develop; release deferred because <work>." and close this bead.
2. Otherwise the publisher bumps the patch version on release/<next-patch>-prep: PR to develop with `rand-lee` as reviewer; when CI is green send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: <next-patch> version bump PR, CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>.".
3. After Rand merges the bump, run publish-preflight to GO, tag the release candidate, and open the develop -> main PR with `rand-lee` as reviewer. When CI is green send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: <version> release PR to main, preflight GO, CI green. Rand, please complete <PR link>.". If preflight or CI cannot go green, send omega-prime@hermes "sc-lint: <version> release blocked: <cause>. <link>" and leave this bead open. No agent merges to develop or main.
"""
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:release"]
needs = ["pr_develop"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "publisher"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
